{{!-- A2's body: a ranked shortlist, the tag strip, then the grid.

	{{> "home/digest" feed=feed}}

The slices are the same shared query A1 reads, taken with {{#foreach}}'s 1-based inclusive
`from`/`to`: position 1 is the masthead lead, 2–5 are the shortlist, 6–14 the grid.

FOUR IN THE SHORTLIST AND NINE IN THE GRID, so this layout draws all fourteen of the window. The
design draws three and eight — twelve — and a layout that draws less than the window leaves the
posts it skips on no page at all, which is the hole home/window.hbs records. The shortlist is a
vertical list, so a fourth row costs the drawing nothing; nine cards also fill three tracks
exactly, where a three-row shortlist would leave a tenth card alone on a fourth row.

WHAT THE PUBLICATION'S PHOTOGRAPHS CHANGE HERE, AND WHAT THEY DO NOT. The shortlist is the same
four rows either way: it is type, and it reads the same on a publication that photographs and one
that does not. The grid is not. Its cards are 5/4 photographs with the image doing the work and no
excerpt under the title — which on a publication with no photographs left title-and-date over
500px of nothing, an **Underset** (CONTEXT.md), twice as wide as the type in it needs.

So when the newest posts carry no image the grid is A1's — home/archive-grid.hbs, called with
`narrow=true` for this narrower column, cards that carry their excerpt and their tier chip and
close on a rule. One card for the imageless case in both layouts, not two drawings of it.

THE CONDITION IS A1'S, UNCHANGED. home/latest.hbs derives it in full — why the test is a date
cutoff rather than an accumulator, why it is `from="2" limit="4"` and never `to="5"`, why the
`+00:00` in `{{published_at}}` is only safe inside the filter's quotes, why the cutoff is `>=`
and takes the lead post in with it, and why the empty result is read with `{{#if}}` rather than
the get's `{{else}}`. Read it there; it is one condition and it now sizes both layouts.
docs/adr/0005 records the rule the two share: an imageless publication is drawn differently, and
no post may be dropped to do it. This layout drops none — its slices never move.

`../../feed`: {{#get}} renders its block with the query's own response as the context, so from
inside the get the window is two frames up — one for the get, one for the {{#foreach}} it sits in.

`{{#if feed.[1]}}` is the one-post case. With a single post the masthead lead IS the publication,
and the shortlist, the tag strip and the grid are all empty — a heading and two rules over
nothing, the **Orphan** docs/adr/0003 says to omit. Index access, so it costs no query.

`{{t "Latest"}}`, which is A1's heading too. The design source titles this section "More from
this week" (`WeeklyDigestSection.astro`) and no theme can know a publication's cadence: on the
Day-one publication these four rows span five weeks. A divergence, recorded in DECISIONS.md.

The rank is `@number`, which {{#foreach}} sets to the item's absolute position in the query
rather than to its index within the slice — so the shortlist is numbered 02, 03, 04, 05 as the
design numbers its own, not 01, 02, 03, 04. The zero-padding is a comparison rather than a
helper: Handlebars has no string padding and Ghost ships none, and `< 10` is the whole rule. --}}
{{#if feed.[1]}}
	<section
		id="latest"
		aria-labelledby="a2-latest"
		class="container pt-14">
		<h2
			id="a2-latest"
			class="font-ui text-muted mb-2 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">{{t "Latest"}}</h2>

		<div class="flex flex-col">
			{{#foreach feed from="2" to="5"}}
				<article
					class="{{post_class}} border-border max-stack:grid-cols-[40px_minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-4 grid grid-cols-[64px_minmax(0,1fr)_auto] items-baseline gap-7 border-t py-[30px]">
					<span class="text-muted font-mono text-xs">{{#match @number "<" 10}}0{{/match}}{{@number}}</span>

					<div>
						<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading text-[27px] leading-[1.22] font-medium">
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="text-text hover:text-accent no-underline">{{title}}</a>
						</h3>

						<p class="text-body text-muted mt-3 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.6] text-pretty">{{excerpt}}</p>

						<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-3.5 uppercase">
							{{~#primary_tag}}{{name}}<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>{{/primary_tag~}}
							{{> "dateline"}}
						</p>
					</div>

					{{> "tier-chip" tight=true}}
				</article>
			{{/foreach}}
		</div>

		{{> "tag-strip" wide=true wrapClass="border-border mt-14 border-t pt-7"}}

		{{#foreach feed from="2" limit="4"}}
			{{#if @last}}
				{{#get "posts" limit="1" filter="published_at:>='{{published_at}}'+feature_image:-null" as |photographed|}}
					{{#if photographed}}
						<div class="border-border mt-11 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-9 gap-y-10 border-t pt-11 lg:grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(360px,100%),1fr))]">
							{{#foreach ../../feed from="6" to="14"}}
								<article class="{{post_class}}">
									<a
										href="{{url}}"
										class="text-text block no-underline">
										{{#if feature_image}}
											<img
												src="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}}"
												{{> "image-srcset" image=feature_image sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 510px, (min-width: 768px) 704px, 100vw"}}
												{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
												loading="lazy"
												decoding="async"
												class="border-border block aspect-[5/4] w-full rounded-md border object-cover">
										{{/if}}

										{{#primary_tag}}
											<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent mt-4 uppercase">{{name}}</p>
										{{/primary_tag}}

										<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading mt-2.5 text-[23px] leading-[1.22] font-medium">{{title}}</h3>

										<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-3 uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</p>
									</a>
								</article>
							{{/foreach}}
						</div>
					{{else}}
						<div class="border-border mt-11 border-t pt-11">
							{{> "home/archive-grid" feed=../../feed start="6" narrow=true}}
						</div>
					{{/if}}
				{{/get}}
			{{/if}}
		{{/foreach}}
	</section>
{{/if}}
